{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Public sector wages to be proportionally linked for inflation & pay gap reduced",
        "additional_details": "In our view, the lowest paid public sector jobs such as nurses and carers have been disproportionately affected by inflation over the past decades and the gap between the best and worst paid has become unacceptably large. Percentage uplifts should be the same for all, up to a maximum of 3 times the monetary value of that received by the lowest paid worker, regardless of grade or profession. We feel there is no justification for such a large gap between the lowest paid workers and executive salaries, which gap the must Government must work to reduce.",
        "background": "All public sector wages should receive the same yearly automatic percentage increase in line with inflation with the total WTE recompense received by any public sector employee (wages, pension contributions, bonuses/other benefits) not exceeding 3 times that of the lowest paid public sector worker.",
